  "title": "the learning rule at length: v44 at book100k / book300k with half the cortex step (lr 0.1) or half the granule NLMS step (granLr 0.05), plus granW 40 at 100k, k 2512-2519 (book300k refs v43 / v44 = y181, same growths)",
  "priority": 0.97,
  "estHours": 2.4,
  "slotHours": 14.6,
  "phone": false,
  "flag": "text",
  "memGB": 1.5,
  "accept": {
    "note": "y162b: the 1x brain is slightly worse at 300k than at 100k (0.394 vs 0.398) and granAnneal does not help; if a smaller main-cortex or granule step lifts 300k above 100k, the plateau is a step-size (rule) problem and an annealed cortex step is the next design."
  },
  "runs": [
